THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

This reservation covers Vapor Music's own work only. The third-party components
it incorporates remain under their own licences, which are not affected by
anything above and are not superseded by it. Those components, their licences
and the attributions they require are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and the
licence texts are in licenses/.

Notably, the audio decoding stack (symphonia) and part of the application shell
(Servo-derived CSS crates, via Tauri) are licensed MPL-2.0. Their terms apply to
those files and are unaffected by this notice. Vapor Music does not modify them.


WHY THIS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT

This is a starting position rather than a settled one, taken because the two
directions are not equally reversible: rights that have not been granted can be
granted later, and rights that have been granted cannot be withdrawn from work
already distributed. Nothing in Vapor Music's dependencies requires it to be
open source — see docs/LICENSING.md for the inventory this rests on — so the
choice is genuinely open, and it is deliberately left open.

docs/LICENSING.md records the route to an open licence, its preconditions, and
what would have to change.
